==Finnish==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*kaďa-|t=to leave}}. Cognates are found in almost every Uralic language, e.g. {{cog|se|guođđit|t=to leave something, to depart}}, {{cog|sms|kue´đđed|t=to leave smth}}, {{cog|mdf|кадомс|t=to leave}}, {{cog|chm|кодаш|t=to stay}}, {{cog|udm|кыльыны|t=to stay}}, {{cog|hu|hagy|t=to let; to leave}}, {{cog|mns|хули|t=to leave}}, {{cog|sel|t=to leave|ts=quəčə-}}. Labialization of the stem vowel occurred in Proto-Finnic, compare {{cog|et|kadu|t=loss}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{hyphenation|ka|to|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|ɑto|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈkɑto]}}

====Noun====
{{fi-noun}}

# [[failure]] of [[crop]]s
# [[loss]], [[disappearance]], [[lack]] {{q|used primarily in compound terms}}
#: {{uxi|fi|[[yleisö]]'''kato'''|'''lack''' or '''loss''' of audience}}

=====Declension=====
{{fi-decl-valo|ka|t|d|o|a}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|fi|kadota|pos=v}}

=====Compounds=====
{{der3|lang=fi|immuunikato|karvakato|katoalue|katokorvaus|katovahinko|katovuosi|kulmakarvakato|luukato|otsonikato|perikato|silmäripsikato|väestökato|yleisökato}}

===Etymology 2===
A dialectal or colloquial 2nd person imperative present of {{m|fi|katsoa||to look}}. The corresponding infinitive is {{m|fi|kattoa}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{hyphenation|ka|to|lang=fi}}
* {{rhymes|ɑto|lang=fi}}
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈkɑtoˣ]}}

====Verb====
{{head|fi|verb form}}

# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} [[look]]!
#: '''''Kato''', tuolla on George!'' &mdash; ''Look, there's George!''
# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} [[see]] (used often with [[nyt|ny]])
#: '''''Kato''' ny, mähän sanoin.'' &mdash; ''See, I told you so.''

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|fi|katso}}
* {{l|fi|ka}} {{qual|colloquial}}

====Interjection====
{{fi-int}}

# {{lb|fi|colloquial}} [[see]] or [[look]].
#* ''Se on '''kato''' sillä lailla.''
#** '''''See''', that’s the way it is.''
#* '''''Kato''' nääs!'' or '''''Kato kato!'''''
#** Literally: ''Look, look!.'' Uttered in surprise, not necessarily telling anyone to look anywhere.
#* '''''Kato nääs''', säkin olet saapunut paikalle.''
#** '''''Lo and behold''', you have arrived on the scene, too.''
#* ''...'''kato''' nääs.'' or ''...'''kato.'''''
#** ''...you see.'' (At the end of a sentence)

=====Synonyms=====
* [[katsos]], [[näet]], [[nimittäin]]

===See also===
